('q-8a3b3fba0f28', 'In the study of relations and functions, what is the ''domain'' of a relation?', 'In the study of relations and functions, what is the ''domain'' of a relation?', '["The set of all first coordinates (inputs) from the ordered pairs", "The set of all second coordinates (outputs) from the ordered pairs", "The graph plotted only on the positive y-axis", "The rule that maps multiple outputs to a single input"]'::jsonb, '["The set of all first coordinates (inputs) from the ordered pairs", "The set of all second coordinates (outputs) from the ordered pairs", "The graph plotted only on the positive y-axis", "The rule that maps multiple outputs to a single input"]'::jsonb, 0, 'As discussed in Unit 1: Relations and Functions (page 11), the domain of a relation consists of the set of all first coordinates of the ordered pairs.', 'As discussed in Unit 1: Relations and Functions (page 11), the domain of a relation consists of the set of all first coordinates of the ordered pairs.', 'ethiopian_science', 'Mathematics', 'medium', 'MATHEMATICS MATHEMATICS', 'Unit 1: Relations and Functions', 11),
('q-4fce715d0b51', 'Which of the following conditions must be satisfied for a relation to be classified as a function?', 'Which of the following conditions must be satisfied for a relation to be classified as a function?', '["Every element in the domain is paired with exactly one element in the range", "Every element in the range must be equal to zero", "The relation must only contain negative integers", "No two distinct inputs can produce the same output value"]'::jsonb, '["Every element in the domain is paired with exactly one element in the range", "Every element in the range must be equal to zero", "The relation must only contain negative integers", "No two distinct inputs can produce the same output value"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Textbook definition (page 12): A function is a relation where each input in the domain maps to exactly one output in the range.', 'Textbook definition (page 12): A function is a relation where each input in the domain maps to exactly one output in the range.', 'ethiopian_science', 'Mathematics', 'medium', 'MATHEMATICS MATHEMATICS', 'Unit 1: Relations and Functions', 12),
('q-fcd75ad4a31d', 'According to Unit 1: Relations and Functions, what is the mathematical definition of ''point where the axes meet''?', 'According to Unit 1: Relations and Functions, what is the mathematical definition of ''point where the axes meet''?', '["It is theorigin of the coordinate system", "The geometric reflection of an arbitrary set across the origin.", "A numerical sequence where consecutive terms differ by a constant ratio.", "The subset of imaginary roots obtained by solving higher-degree polynomials."]'::jsonb, '["It is theorigin of the coordinate system", "The geometric reflection of an arbitrary set across the origin.", "A numerical sequence where consecutive terms differ by a constant ratio.", "The subset of imaginary roots obtained by solving higher-degree polynomials."]'::jsonb, 0, 'Based on the text on page 14: the point where the axes meet
is called theorigin of the coordinate system.', 'Based on the text on page 14: the point where the axes meet
